# Standalone guided walk through bob/capture — a SearchTextRequest whose
# type was inferred, whose score is not perfect, and whose first text_query
# is shadowed by a second.
#
# Invocation:
#   protolens --descriptor-set alice/app.desc \
#       --script grpconf2026/beats/capture.script bob/capture
#
# Positional paths:
#   /    SearchTextRequest root (inferred, score −8)
#   /1   text_query: "<binary blob>"  — the shadowed first instance
#   /2   text_query: "coffee in Grenoble"  #@ repeated_singular
#   /3   language_code: "en-US"
#
# Re-pin (must print nothing):
#   protolens --descriptor-set alice/app.desc \
#       --script grpconf2026/beats/capture.script bob/capture script \
#     | grep 'error:'

title: What is bob/capture?

steps:
  - text: |
      bob/capture, opened against alice/app.desc.

      As you can see, protolens renders the capture as textproto format,
      enriched with annotations (press `a` to hide/show them).

      It also correctly inferred the type of the protobuf.

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /
    select_line: true
    search: SearchTextRequest

  - text: |
      Cheat sheet:
      - navigate with arrow keys and the mouse
      - fold/unfold messages by pressing `z` or clicking the triangles
      - press `w` to show the wire-level bytes
      - hover over text for more information

      👋 Exercise: fold the location_bias message and click the root node to step.

    node: /
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - node: /
      - not:
        - visible: /7/1

  - text: |
      Hover over the root type and we get the full type name and a score:
      the protobuf has 12 wire-level fields matching the type,
      but takes a 20-point penalty for a non-canonical encoding.

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /
    fold: ["/ 1"]
    select_line: true
    search: SearchTextRequest

  - text: |
      Indeed, there is a problem with the text_query field: in the decompiled
      .proto it is not declared as a repeated field (press `v` for the viewer),
      yet it has two instances in the protobuf.

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /2
    fold: ["/ 1"]
    select_line: true
    search: text_query

  - text: |
      protolens flags the second instance with an amber diamond
      and a `repeated_singular` annotation.

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /2
    fold: ["/ 1"]
    select_line: true
    search: repeated_singular

  - text: |
      The first instance is shadowed by the second:
      a standard decoder like protoc will silently drop it.

      protolens flags it with a hollow amber diamond...

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /1
    fold: ["/ 1"]
    select_line: true

  - text: |
      The first instance is shadowed by the second:
      a standard decoder like protoc will silently drop it.

      protolens flags it with a hollow amber diamond
      and a `shadowed_scalar` annotation.

      👋 Press space to step.

    node: /1
    fold: ["/ 1"]
    select_line: true
    search: shadowed_scalar

  - text: |
      So bob/capture is a SearchTextRequest — with a non-canonical encoding 🤔.

      Let's have a look at the downloaded log file.

      👋 Press Enter to quit.

    node: /1
    fold: ["/ 1"]
    select_line: true
    command: quit
